e} operation leverages the 	extit{improve\_prompt} to instruct the LLM to improve a merged NDA. First, we present the prompt stubs (Table ef{tab:doc_prompt_stubs} - Table ef{tab:doc_prompt_stubs_continued}), serving as templates to dynamically generate appropriate prompts at runtime. Following this, we outline the LLM interactions throughout a complete merging process (Table ef{tab:doc_example_nda12} - Table ef{tab:doc_example_finale}). However, instead of displaying each input/generated NDA in every prompt/response, we present the 4 input NDAs in Table ef{tab:doc_example_nda12} - Table ef{tab:doc_example_nda4} and the final merged NDA in Table ef{tab:doc_example_finale}. Furthermore, as scoring is done using the LLM as well, we will present these interactions for the best performing merged NDAs (Tables ef{tab:doc_example_scoring} - ef{tab:doc_example_scoring_r} and Tables ef{tab:doc_example_scoring_s3} - ef{tab:doc_example_scoring_s3_r}). Lastly, most responses are limited to a few lines only, as they don't offer any further insights and would otherwise span multiple pages. However, we refer the interested reader to the results in the corresponding code repository ootnote{https://github.com/spcl/graph-of-thoughts} for full logs and further examples.  egin{table*} \centering enewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.5} \caption{Prompt stubs for the document merging task; parameters in single curly brackets will be substituted at runtime.} \label{tab:doc_prompt_stubs}  egin{tabularx}{	extwidth}{X} \hline 	extbf{merge\_prompt:} Merge the following 4 NDA documents 	extless{}Doc1	extgreater{} - 	extless{}Doc4	extgreater{} into a single NDA, maximizing retained information and minimizing redundancy. Output only the created NDA between the tags 	extless{}Merged	extgreater{} and 	extless{}/Merged	extgreater{}, without any additional text. \ Here are NDAs 	extless{}Doc1	extgreater{} - 	extless{}Doc4	extgreater{}: \ 	extless{}Doc1	extgreater{} \{doc1\} 	extless{}/Doc1	extgrea